.TH KIRO-HWD 8 "2026-11-28" "kiro-hwd" "Kiro system tools"
.SH NAME
kiro-hwd \- pick and install the NVIDIA driver for this machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiro-hwd
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.br
.B kiro-hwd detect
.br
.B kiro-hwd install
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B kiro-hwd power
.br
.B kiro-hwd flip\-fix
.RB [ \-\-no\-initramfs ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiro-hwd
reads the display devices from sysfs, looks up each NVIDIA device ID in the PCI ID lists mirrored from
CachyOS chwd, and picks one of Kiro's driver profiles:
.TP
.B nvidia-580xx
Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards (the nvidia-580 list).
.TP
.B nouveau
Kepler and older (the nvidia-470, nvidia-390 and nouveau lists): nothing is installed, the open nouveau
driver stays.
.TP
.B nvidia-open
every other NVIDIA card (Turing and newer).
.PP
A laptop (chassis type 8, 9, 10, 11 or 31) with an Intel or AMD iGPU next to the NVIDIA card also gets
nvidia-prime and switcheroo-control for render offload. kiro-hwd does not switch GPU modes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B detect
Show the GPUs, the chosen profile and why. Needs no root.
.TP
.B install
Upgrade the system, then install the profile's packages. Each package comes from the first repo that has it:
the Arch repos, then chaotic-aur, then cachyos. When [cachyos] is commented out in /etc/pacman.conf, a temporary
copy with it enabled is used; /etc/pacman.conf is never changed. Kiro supports x86_64 only, so no 32-bit (lib32)
packages are installed. Writes /etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/10-kiro-hwd.conf (early NVIDIA modules) and, on desktops,
10-kiro-hwd-kms.conf (drops the kms hook), and records the result in /var/lib/kiro-hwd/state. Stops when
another NVIDIA driver branch is installed. Run mkinitcpio -P afterwards (the Kiro installer does this).
.TP
.B install \-\-dry\-run
Show the packages and the repo each comes from; install nothing. Needs no root.
.TP
.B power
Write /etc/modprobe.d/10-kiro-hwd-nvidia.conf (NVreg_DynamicPowerManagement=0x02) on a Turing laptop, remove it
everywhere else. Runs on a kiro-hwd upgrade.
.TP
.B flip\-fix
While the installed nvidia-utils is a 620.x build, write /etc/modprobe.d/11-kiro-hwd-flip.conf
(options nvidia_modeset opportunistic_flip_sync=0) against NVIDIA bug 7126445: a black screen at the Wayland login
with two or more screens. Otherwise remove it. When the file changed and nvidia is in the initramfs
(10-kiro-hwd.conf), run mkinitcpio -P, unless
.B \-\-no\-initramfs
is given. Run by /usr/share/libalpm/hooks/60-kiro-hwd-flip.hook (with \-\-no\-initramfs: a driver change also triggers
the mkinitcpio hook, which rebuilds after DKMS) whenever nvidia-utils is installed, upgraded or removed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KIRO_HWD_SYSFS, KIRO_HWD_CHASSIS
For testing only: read the PCI devices from another directory and use this chassis type.
.TP
.B KIRO_HWD_MODPROBE_DIR
For testing only: write the modprobe.d files to another directory (no initramfs rebuild then).
.SH FILES
.TP
/usr/share/kiro-hwd/profiles.toml
Kiro's driver profiles.
.TP
/usr/share/kiro-hwd/ids/
PCI ID lists from CachyOS chwd (GPL-3.0-or-later); UPSTREAM names the synced commit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR mkinitcpio (8)
